{
  "patient_information": "A 4-year-old girl, previously healthy, from rural eastern Uganda.",
  "chief_complaint": "Unconscious and in a coma.",
  "history_of_present_illness": "Well until yesterday, then developed a bad headache in the early afternoon, followed by shaking chills in the evening; family believed it was another episode of malaria; child slept restlessly; at 5 a.m. today the family woke to find the girl was in the midst of a seizure, which lasted about ten minutes; it took 4 hours for the family to reach A&E and the child has not awoken; no recent head trauma and no other known reason for the child to be ill.",
  "exposure_and_epidemiology": "It is the rainy season in rural eastern Uganda, where malaria is a common problem in their village; people living in this area of high malaria transmission may be frequently bitten by malaria-infected female anopheline mosquitoes.",
  "vitals": "Temperature 38.7°C (101.7°F), pulse 150 bpm, respiratory rate 36 breath cycles per minute, blood pressure 98/40 mmHg.",
